  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool and the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, mediated through intermediate targets. Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool is directly linked to CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which in turn is targeted by 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide and also by (4As,10As)-1,1,4A-Trimethyl-7-Propan-2-Yl-2,3,4,9,10,10A-Hexahydrophenanthrene. Both of these compounds are implicated in targeting the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. The scores for the pathways indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, suggesting that Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool may influence the proteasome through these intermediates. The evidence highlights a possible role in proteasome regulation, though the exact mechanism and the extent of Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool's involvement remain to be fully elucidated.",
